<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--ThermalHAL config for mocha.

     The service reads this file as /vendor/etc/thermalhal.<ro.hardware>.xml,
     and ro.hardware here is tn8: the board carries NVIDIA's TN8 BSP, which is
     why fstab.tn8 and ueventd.tn8.rc are named the way they are too.

     Every zone below is named by its type string in /sys/class/thermal, which
     the kernel takes from the device tree node. CPU-therm and GPU-therm are
     soctherm sensors, therm_est is the estimated skin temperature, battery is
     the fuel gauge's own zone. All four report milli-degrees, hence the
     multiplier.

     The thresholds are not written here: the HAL reads them from the zone's
     own trip points, taking the first "passive" trip for both throttling
     thresholds and "critical" for shutdown. Only the two soctherm zones have
     both. The skin estimator has a single passive trip at 47C and no critical
     one, and the battery zone has no trips at all, so both borrow CPU-therm's
     thresholds through threshold-label. This is not cosmetic: a zone whose
     four paths cannot all be resolved makes the HAL refuse the entire list,
     not just that zone.

     No cores attribute. It repeats one reading once per core and tells the
     framework nothing the single CPU entry does not.

     No cooling devices. The tablet is passively cooled: no pwm-fan node
     appears anywhere in the device trees mocha includes, and FAN_RPM is the
     only cooling type this interface knows.

     One honest oddity to expect on a cold device: therm_est reports 25C until
     the board sensor passes 40C and the estimator starts. That is the
     estimator working as designed, not a dead zone.
-->
<thermalhal>
	<thermal_devices>
		<thermal_device>
			<thermal-prop name="CPU" type="DEVICE_TEMPERATURE_CPU" sensor-label="CPU-therm" multiplier='0.001' />
		</thermal_device>
		<thermal_device>
			<thermal-prop name="GPU" type="DEVICE_TEMPERATURE_GPU" sensor-label="GPU-therm" multiplier='0.001' />
		</thermal_device>
		<thermal_device>
			<thermal-prop name="skin" type="DEVICE_TEMPERATURE_SKIN" sensor-label="therm_est" threshold-label="CPU-therm" multiplier='0.001' />
		</thermal_device>
		<thermal_device>
			<thermal-prop name="battery" type="DEVICE_TEMPERATURE_BATTERY" sensor-label="battery" threshold-label="CPU-therm" multiplier='0.001' />
		</thermal_device>
	</thermal_devices>
	<cpu_usages cpus="4" />
</thermalhal>
